        {
          "LayerName": "TRT - 00:19 Date - 05/07/2023 KSC Contact - Leejay Lockhart (32",
          "LayerText": "TRT - 00:19 Date - 05/07/2023 KSC Contact - Leejay Lockhart (321) 867-2468 More Info (website): www.nasa.gov/kennedy    "
        },
        {
          "LayerName": "Orbital ATK dedicated its next Cygnus spacecraft to Sen. John G",
          "LayerText": "Orbital ATK dedicated its next Cygnus spacecraft to Sen. John Glenn, one of NASA’s  original seven astronauts and an ardent supporter of spaceflight.  NASA, Orbital ATK and United Launch Alliance officials spoke about the importance  of the flight during a break in processing work inside the Payload Hazardous Servicing  Facility at NASA’s Kennedy Space Center in Florida. The spacecraft is targeted to launch  March 19 at 10:56 p.m. EDT aboard a United Launch Alliance Atlas V rocket.  It will carry more than 7,600 pounds of supplies to the International Space Station  including experiments across a wide range of sciences, equipment for the station and  supplies for the crew. The mission will be station’s second cargo delivery of 2017 and  Orbital ATK’s seventh contracted resupply mission for NASA. "
        },
        {
          "LayerName": "Orbital ATK Dedicates Cygnus Spacecraft to John Glenn",
          "LayerText": "Orbital ATK Dedicates Cygnus Spacecraft to John Glenn"
        },
